internal/fleet/soldier_manifest.go	CheckLegacyBriefMigration	1	!isWithinWorktreeRoot(worktreePath, realPath)	BEO-69: a post-check against a race, not an unreachable branch. Premise: legacyPath is the fixed direct child filepath.Join(worktreePath, ".soldier-md"); the preceding Lstat rejects a symlink and every non-regular child, so a stable regular child resolves to a path lexically inside the resolved root. EvalSymlinks(worktreeRoot) failure also cannot reach this comparison because Lstat(legacyPath) fails first. Probed direct-child symlink and directory rejection, symlinked-root canonicalization, an outside hard link (which remains lexically inside), and an unresolved root; all refuse or resolve before containment. Only replacing a checked path component between Lstat and EvalSymlinks can enter this branch. Pinned by TestGuardBurnDownManifestContainmentWaiversPinned. Invalidate if the child becomes caller-supplied or nested, the preceding checks are removed or reordered, root canonicalization changes, or filesystem access becomes injectable/atomic enough to deterministically substitute a component between the syscalls.
